[09:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This tells us that the prompt and the reference video are equally important in guiding the final result There’s another possible reason as well The original video may be around nine seconds long while our current output is only five seconds'

[09:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'When the source and output durations don’t align that can also lead to weaker video-editing results Now let’s look at prop replacement In the original video the woman twists open the cap of a bottle of mineral water and then drinks from it'

[09:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
